Greetings,

I am using l3build lately and noticed that the date printed in the =
document title (if \date is not used) using e.g.
 =20
	texlua build.lua doc

for compilation is wrong. Instead of the current date (which would today =
be =E2=80=9EApril 20, 2018=E2=80=9C) I get =E2=80=9EMay 20, 2016=E2=80=9C.=

Interestingly, if I compile the .dtx file directly (using e.g. pdflatex) =
I get the correct date.

I don=E2=80=99t know if I do something wrong =E2=80=A6 but here are the =
documents I use:

My reduced test .dtx file:
	% \iffalse=20
	%<*driver>=20
	\documentclass{l3doc}
=09
	\begin{document}
	\DocInput{\jobname.dtx}
	\end{document}
	%</driver>
	% \fi
	% \GetFileInfo{\jobname.sty}
	% \title{The \pkg{\jobname} package}
	% \maketitle
	%=20
	% \begin{documentation}
	% \end{documentation}
	%
	% \begin{implementation}
	%    \begin{macrocode}
	\def\Versuch{Versuch}
	%    \end{macrocode}
	%\end{implementation}

The .ins file:
	\input l3docstrip.tex
	\askforoverwritefalse
	\generate{\file{\jobname.sty}{\from{\jobname.dtx}{package}}}
	\endbatchfile

And the build.lua file:
	#!/usr/bin/env texlua
=09
	module =3D "test"
=09
	kpse.set_program_name("kpsewhich")
	dofile(kpse.lookup("l3build.lua=E2=80=9C))

I am currently using the 2018/02/20 version of l3build and texlive2017. =
Do I need to specify the printed date somewhere?

Ben


